From 84e23547d456abc03c894c6ae42776d84278ad8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(admission): ride out a briefly busy update lock instead
 of refusing turns [daveey]

A busy admission.lock (hermes-sync's state read, its hold write, a Kanban claim
through its commit) got the same refusal as a real update hold after one 50 ms
try, so a Desktop message, notification or goal turn was dropped and logged as
'Update admission unavailable' with a TimeoutError traceback (agent-6f2f71c662).

- admission_fence: lock timeout raises AdmissionBusy(TimeoutError).
- backend_retirement.reservation(busy_wait_s=0.5) / begin_background_review
  retry AdmissionBusy in 50 ms tries; a hold or retirement still refuses at once.
  prompt.admit (under the session resume lock) passes busy_wait_s=0 and warm
  session.resume uses single_lock_try(), so both keep one 50 ms try.
- A final busy refusal logs one WARNING 'update admission lock busy for Ns (no
  update hold)' without a traceback; recovered contention logs DEBUG.
- prompt.submit / side-agent 5035 text says 'briefly busy; retry' for that case.
